#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:478
msgid "Challenges When Accepting All TypeForms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:480
msgid ""
"A function that takes an *arbitrary* ``TypeForm`` as input must support a "
"variety of possible type form objects. Such functions are not easy to write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:483
msgid ""
"New special forms are introduced with each new Python version, and special "
"handling may be required for each one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:485
msgid ""
"Quoted annotations [#quoted_less_common]_ (like ``'list[str]'``) must be "
"*parsed* (to something like ``list[str]``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:487
msgid ""
"Resolving quoted forward references inside type expressions is typically "
"done with ``eval()``, which is difficult to use in a safe way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:489
msgid ""
"Recursive types like ``IntTree = list[int | 'IntTree']`` are difficult to "
"resolve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0747.rst:491
msgid ""
"User-defined generic types (like Django’s ``QuerySet[User]``) can introduce "
"non-standard behaviors that require runtime support."
msgstr ""

